WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.401 --> 00:00:04.318
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.030
- We've had to go above and beyond

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.045
to keep these people safe.

00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:32.700
I mean, end of the day,
these people are our family

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.870
and they work with us and for us

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.880
and we have to take care of them.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.430
It's our responsibility.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.330
- [Alejandro] While farms adapt

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.770
to coronavirus safety measures

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.650
in the field, foreign farm workers

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.480
are often returning to crowded housing

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.770
where outbreaks have already spread.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.670
What is the agricultural industry doing

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.130
to protect its guest farm workers?

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.890
According to local news reports,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.840
outbreaks have torn through
guest worker housing

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.170
across the country,

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.136
infecting more than 500 farm workers

00:00:58.136 --> 00:01:00.130
and killing at least six.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.660
One outbreak was here
at this converted motel,

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.610
owned by Alco Harvesting
in Santa Maria, California

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.530
where roughly 250 farm workers live.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.720
In July, 104 workers were infected here

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.185
and one later died according
to country health officials.

00:01:14.185 --> 00:01:18.102
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:30.418 --> 00:01:32.460
- [Alejandro] Current Alco
workers like Luis Sanchez

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.720
say they were scared

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.600
but they say Alco did everything it could

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.150
to control the outbreak.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.840
Sanchez was infected though he says

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.530
he didn't have any symptoms.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.380
But Jesus Guzman, a
former worker with Alco

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.023
was more critical of the
company's safety measures.

00:01:57.373 --> 00:01:59.060
- [Alejandro] Guzman says he
was living in a room like this

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.010
with five other workers
when the outbreak began.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.160
As the disease spread, Guzman
says Alco withheld details

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.269
about who was sick and how
they were being cared for.

00:02:08.269 --> 00:02:12.186
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.810
- [Alejandro] He says he was fired

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.560
when he asked for time off to quarantine

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.400
after getting a test on his own

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.330
and later tested positive.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.930
- The PPEs, the social distancing,

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.680
the amount of time and
energy we had to spend

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.920
to make sure everyone
was safe, it took a lot.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.190
And we're still learning.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.660
- [Alejandro] Alco's general
manager, Jeremy MacKenzie,

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.335
said that the company's safety protocols,

00:02:42.335 --> 00:02:45.100
like mandated masks, social distancing

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.215
and disinfecting worked
to contain the outbreak.

00:02:48.215 --> 00:02:49.220
- The people we spoke to said

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.611
that there wasn't available testing

00:02:51.611 --> 00:02:56.010
and that some workers were
even retaliated against

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.780
when they said that
the outbreak was larger

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.510
than what you were saying publicly.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.620
I'd really like you to respond to that.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.540
- Yeah, I mean, testing
was tough for everybody.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.840
We were getting people
in as soon as we could.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.960
Retaliation is something we don't do.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.363
So that is not a true statement.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.990
We take care of our employees

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.950
and look out for their best
interests at all times.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.150
- [Alejandro] In a written statement,

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.580
MacKenzie added, "Despite much effort,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.020
we have felt the deep sadness

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.100
of losing an employee,
and our hearts go out

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.940
to all the families how
have lost a loved one

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.283
during this pandemic.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.560
Most of the farm workers
living at the Alco motel

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.780
were from Mexico,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.573
working through a growing
program called H-2A.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.250
H-2A employers like Alco tend

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.220
to fill local motels that
they own or rent with workers.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.660
H-2A rules require only 50
square feet of sleeping space

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.720
for each worker.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.100
A requirement that hasn't been
revised during the pandemic.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.030
The Centers for Disease Control
and Prevention recommend

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.870
keeping six feet apart from people

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.530
but because the workers all
travel and work together,

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.683
social distancing can be more challenging.

00:04:04.719 --> 00:04:08.636
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:19.027 --> 00:04:20.510
- [Alejandro] Guzman says Alco let him go,

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.550
even though he was entitled to six leave

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.270
and wanted to return to work.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.210
The recently filed a
compliant against Alco

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.110
for labor code violations.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.009
Alco told The Wall Street
Journal that quote,

00:04:30.009 --> 00:04:33.490
"The company has only ever
terminated a worker's employment

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:36.210
for actionable reasons allowed by law."

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.040
Hazel Davalos, a local
farm worker advocate,

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.096
says Guzman's story

00:04:40.096 --> 00:04:42.610
was one she heard a lot about the outbreak

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.150
at Alco's motel.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.480
- We've been shared countless
stories from workers

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.410
around when they've asked

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.740
for temperature checks and screenings.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.670
They've been told if you
don't like it, you can leave.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.910
That sort of attitude.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.450
We learned after the
Alco Harvesting outbreak

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.520
that resulted in over 90
workers infected with COVID.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.920
That many of those workers
were told go back to work

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.140
if you're not showing symptoms.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.970
- [Alejandro] Research shows
farm workers have been hit

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.030
especially hard by COVID-19.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.390
Purdue University researchers estimate

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.830
that more than 185,000 farm workers

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.640
have contracted the virus.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.920
The agricultural industry
says it's been adapting

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.350
to the pandemic as quickly as it can.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.780
The Grower-Shipper Association

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.660
of Central California started offering

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.760
quarantine housing for farm workers.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.330
Several states have passed orders,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.260
requiring farm workers to be tested.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.600
And Santa Barbara County in California,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.810
where Alco is based,

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.940
recently passed an ordinance requiring

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.300
that guest workers be
tested daily for symptoms,

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.980
self-quarantine if exposed

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.350
and that employers
report all positive cases

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.800
to the Health Department.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:46.633
- During the pandemic,

00:05:46.633 --> 00:05:48.800
just seeing a simple policy

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.620
that says workers need to be tested

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.940
upon arrival to the country

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.240
and tested regularly,

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.450
need to be transported in small levels,

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:57.730
those same sort of health orders

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:58.879
that we've seen locally,

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:02.260
seeing those nationally I
think would be effective.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.600
- [Alejandro] The Occupational Safety

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.730
and Health Administration

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.800
is currently investigating
the Alco worker's death.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.590
Alco says they had already
implemented the safety measures

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.000
now required locally

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.630
and that they've updated their
protocols since the outbreak.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:17.093
- We temperature check
everybody every morning.

00:06:17.093 --> 00:06:20.510
Hand sanitizer before you get on the bus,

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.670
at breaks, at lunch.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.750
It's readily available everywhere.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.570
We hand out many hand sanitizers

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.053
for all their pockets,
masks for everybody.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.098
Our protocols have changed dramatically.

00:06:35.098 --> 00:06:39.015
(speaking in foreign language)

00:07:01.513 --> 00:07:04.263
(dramatic music)

